WEBVTT

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:05.230
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.530
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:39.600
Don’t let any Pokémon Hunters
capture you again.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.150
I’ve never seen
that look on your face before.

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:52.440
The Alolan Kyukon
should be fine now.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.700
Any leads on the Hunters?

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:56.910
We’ve found them.
We’ll head their way next.

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:01.700
Aren’t you curious about the trainer
who caught that Kyukon?

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:07.080
It was your choice to pass him
after he got disqualified, right?

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.590
So, what?

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:14.630
Nothing. He’s about to start
his first Trial Mission.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:16.090
Whatever.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:23.100
Oh, please.
He’s <i>obviously</i> curious.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.980
Ooh! It’s here, it’s here!

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:31.570
My first trial mission
from Project Mew is here!

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.030
So? What’s it say?

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:40.700
Umm... “Reach the goal by making
full use of a variety of Pokémon.”

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.990
Huh? There’s three of them!

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:42.700
Huh?

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:43.540
Three?

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:46.750
It says I can choose
whichever one I like.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.040
Hmm...

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:52.050
Okay, I pick this one!

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:54.960
“Gather Ulgamoth’s golden scales!”

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:56.920
Ulgamoth, huh...?

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:57.340
Wait...

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:00.220
But what’s it mean by
“golden scales”...?

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:03.850
That would appear to be
the key to this mission.

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:07.020
Kikuna, display its Index data
on the main monitor.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:07.730
Right away.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:14.280
Ulgamoth. Sun Pokémon.
Bug/Fire type.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.900
It hatches from a cocoon
formed of raging flames.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:22.370
It uses its six wings to scatter its Ember scales,
igniting a sea of fire that engulfs its surroundings.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:25.240
So those Ember scales
are golden?

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:29.870
Or maybe it really <i>does</i> scatter
scales made of gold sometimes.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:34.460
They must want you
to figure that out, and clear the mission.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:35.760
Okay!

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.010
The place with the most
info about Ulgamoth...

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:42.220
It’s the Resort Desert in Isshu!

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:43.720
Oh, isn’t that where...?

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:47.600
Yeah! Where I caught Golugh
at the Ruins of the Titan!

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.850
And there was a golden room there!

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:54.190
So there could be an Ulgamoth
with golden scales, too!

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:55.440
That’s great!

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.490
Then let’s head straight to Isshu!

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:59.610
Let’s go!

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:44.760
Go and Satoshi have arrived
at the Ruins of the Titan in Isshu...

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:49.010
...to attempt Project Mew’s
first Trial Mission.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.230
It’s gold and shiny!

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:57.440
Ruins truly are <i>enchanting!</i>

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:00.820
Chief!
We’re looking for Ulgamoth!

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:05.030
Go looked it up and saw that
there were tons of sightings around here!

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:08.820
Hmm... All of that ended
a few days ago, though.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:09.530
Huh?

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:10.910
Did something happen?

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:12.580
Pokémon Hunters.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:17.380
They’ve been using cruel methods
to capture Pokémon nearby.

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:21.170
Ulgamoth seems to have
stopped visiting because of that.

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:23.050
That’s awful!

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:31.010
But my excavation team have made
an <i>enchanting</i> Ulgamoth-related discovery!

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.650
A mural with Ulgamoth...

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:41.360
I wonder what it says...

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:45.280
“When the rage of the mountain
swallows the sky,

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:50.370
“the god of fire shall appear,
to save those suffering from cold.”

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:53.580
The god of fire...
Does that mean Ulgamoth?

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:54.830
I think so.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:58.580
And if the “rage of the mountain”
means an erupting volcano,

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:01.000
then maybe Ulgamoth
is in a volcanic area!

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.380
Indeed.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:09.010
Past these ruins, there’s a town founded in the gold rush,
which was sealed off when a volcano erupted.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:13.100
You might find something
<i>enchanting</i> there!

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.060
Let’s check it out!

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:14.970
Yeah!

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.640
The whole town is falling apart...

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:23.770
Is there really anything
“enchanting” here?

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:27.360
There’s just a huge volcano...

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:36.540
Is this a tunnel
they used to mine gold?

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.330
Let’s move, Go!

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:40.830
Naturally!

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.090
Oh, it’s just some Koromori...

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:51.420
A-Anyway,
I thought this might happen!

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:53.930
So I came prepared, yeah!

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:03.270
Is something there?

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:07.610
A Dangoro?

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:11.780
Dangoro! Mantle Pokémon!
Rock type!

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:15.740
It was discovered a hundred years ago in
an earthquake fissure in a layer of exposed rock!

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:19.120
The material that makes up its body
is dirt from several hundred years ago!

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:25.000
You can leave this battle to me!

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:28.210
Stop! I’ll do it.

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:31.800
Dangoro is a Rock-type,
so I’ll use you, a Water-type!

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:38.800
Inteleon! Snipe Shot!

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:45.230
It worked!

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:47.690
Monster Ball, go!

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:57.490
Dangoro’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:59.290
All right!

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:03.420
Something’s coming!

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:07.380
It’s a horde of Dangoro!

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:13.760
Run for it!

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:16.470
Satoshi!

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:17.720
Okay!

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:41.950
The rails are gone!

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:46.420
Inteleon,
aim for the points lever!

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:55.300
Y-You saved us...

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:57.340
Good work, Inteleon!

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:05.390
It looks like an elevator.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:10.440
Maybe if it still had electricity...

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.150
In that case...

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:13.280
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:23.870
Just what we needed,
Pikachu!

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:35.130
It took us to a big, open place.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:44.640
What’s that?!

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:50.270
Nutrey! Thorn Pod Pokémon!
Grass/Steel type!

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:53.030
Its spikes are harder than steel!

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:58.320
If I’m fighting a Grass/Steel type...
I’ll use you, a Fire type!

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:03.660
Aceburn! Pyro Ball!

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:09.330
It’s super effective!

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:12.840
Go! Monster Ball!

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:20.590
All right!

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:22.430
That’s your second catch today!

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:25.100
Yeah! Thank you, Aceburn!

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:31.020
Oh, thanks for the help.

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:35.030
I’m studying the wild Pokémon
living in this area.

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:38.450
We’re Research Fellows
at Sakuragi Institute.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:39.410
I’m Satoshi!

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:40.160
And I’m Go!

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:42.740
So you’re here to investigate too?

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:45.040
Yes. We’re looking for Ulgamoth.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:49.920
Oh... Actually,
I’m looking for Ulgamoth too.

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:52.710
What do you say?
Why not come with me?

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:53.880
Sure!

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:54.920
That’s okay, right, Go?

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:55.920
S-Sure...

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:57.840
Okay, it’s a deal.

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:02.180
Where are we...?

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:04.810
It’s like a train station...

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:06.850
It’s a mining railway station.

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:11.400
Back during the gold rush,
these tunnels led to the next mine over.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:12.770
You really know a lot.

00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:14.690
Wha—? Oh, not at all...

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:16.530
What are these?

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:18.570
Eggs!

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:21.360
I wonder what eggs these are...

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:23.700
Lemme have a look.

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:27.160
These are probably Melarva eggs.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:32.210
Melarva will hatch from them
and evolve into Ulgamoth.

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:37.380
Are the eggs gonna be okay
just left here on their own, though?

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:39.970
Oh! Then Ulgamoth
might be here!

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:41.340
So it can protect the eggs!

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:42.510
Of course!

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:46.720
Yeah. So before it comes back...

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:49.810
...I better get outta here
with these eggs!

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:50.930
Sticky Web!

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:58.480
What’re you doing?!

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:03.700
While I was catching
all the Pokémon ‘round here,

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:06.870
Ulgamoth managed to get away.

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:10.750
But if I sell all these eggs,
I’ll make plenty of money!

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:13.370
You’re a Pokémon Hunter?!

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:17.750
You just sit tight there...

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:20.340
...till I’ve taken all of these eggs!

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:22.230
We’d never let you!

00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:24.300
You...!

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:42.190
Stop!

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:43.490
Shut it.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:46.820
You just wait patiently there
till I’m finished.

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:50.370
There could be
more eggs down there...

00:12:58.460 --> 00:12:59.590
Melarva!

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:02.670
Two of them!
They’ll fetch a good price...

00:13:02.670 --> 00:13:05.010
Dentula! Sticky Web!

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:13.350
Argh, dammit!

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:14.850
How do you like <i>this,</i> then?!

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:21.150
There’s another one?

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:28.570
Gah! I give up on the Melarva!

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:31.620
Give those eggs back!

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:33.790
Don’t you see
the Melarva are mad?!

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:37.120
These are valuable!
Who’d give them up?

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:44.720
The eggs are gonna
end up burning!

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:48.050
The Melarva are
going crazy with rage!

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:50.550
We’re in danger, too!

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:53.140
No, this could be good!

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:56.310
I get it!

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:01.070
Nearly there...

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:09.950
Satoshi, get the eggs.

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:11.490
I’ll stop the Melarva!

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:13.080
Okay!

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:14.750
Stop, Melarva!

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:17.620
If you keep going,
you’ll burn the eggs!

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:21.970
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:29.380
You still wanna fight?!

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:33.510
You’ll regret this!

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:36.100
Go!

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:40.440
Look! They’re right here!
Your eggs are safe!

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:43.400
So please, stop!

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:47.400
Don’t!

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:49.150
Stop! You have to stop, Melarva!

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:53.450
Watch out, Go!

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:02.670
You understood?

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:06.630
Here, we’re giving the eggs back.

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:09.300
Sorry about this, Melarva.

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:18.140
But... Go...

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:20.440
If this keeps burning...

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:21.650
Right!

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:24.270
You’re up!

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:30.200
I choose you!

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:34.030
Inteleon, use Snipe Shot!

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:35.620
Crab, use Bubble Beam!

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:37.580
Uonoragon! Water Gun!

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:47.130
It’s not working...?

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:49.090
One more try!

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:07.570
That’s the one from the tunnel!

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:14.070
It’s alternate-color...?!

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:20.120
It’s evolving...?!

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:41.560
A golden Ulgamoth!

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:55.530
The flames are being sucked
into the Fire Vortex!

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:56.870
Wow!

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:07.790
It’s gone...

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:18.300
Are these...
the golden scales?

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:19.640
Go!

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:20.260
Right!

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:33.690
I got Ulgamoth’s golden scales!

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.280
You did it, Go!

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:44.620
That’s a strong wind...

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:46.370
Good work.

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:48.500
You again...!

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:49.840
You were still here?!

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:51.670
Of course!

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:56.590
The eggs, the Melarva, and a super-rare golden Ulgamoth...
I’d never give up on those!

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:58.390
How do you...?!

00:17:58.390 --> 00:17:59.970
I was watching.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:03.520
That would sell for a fortune.

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:05.730
So I waited here.

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:07.770
Even called in some friends.

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:25.120
Hand over all
the Pokémon you have.

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:27.410
I’ll make sure they all get sold.

00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:29.170
You’re awful...

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:30.670
You’re not getting away with this!

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:32.840
I’m not, am I?

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:33.710
Sludge Bomb!

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:39.930
What’s wrong?

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:41.010
Weren’t you gonna stop me?

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:48.690
You’re so pitiful.

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:54.690
Ms. Asahi!

00:18:55.190 --> 00:18:59.700
But the most pitiful things here
are the Pokémon doing your dirty work.

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:01.160
Right.

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:03.780
The Pokémon aren’t to blame.

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:04.700
Mr. Tsurugi!

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:07.790
And who are you?
Their friends?

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:09.710
Zip it. Your words foul the air.

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:10.580
What?!

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:12.630
Let’s get this started.

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:15.550
I’ll take those three.

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:17.360
Don’t you belittle me...

00:19:17.360 --> 00:19:18.300
Hit ‘em with Crunch!

00:19:20.180 --> 00:19:21.390
Use Poison Jab!

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:24.140
Go, Wulaosu!

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:30.020
You, too!

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:36.530
Pouring Strikes!

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:44.870
Wulaosu! Dark Blow!

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:00.920
Two Wulaosu!

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:03.550
And that one’s different from
Mr. Tsurugi’s Single Strike Form!

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:09.810
Wulaosu! Rapid Strike Form! Martial Arts Pokémon!
Fighting/Water type!

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:17.480
It’s believed that this Pokémon modeled its fighting style
on the flow of a river—sometimes rapid, sometimes calm!

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:18.780
You’re both okay?

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:20.150
Yeah!

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:23.660
Go, you chose
the golden scales, right?

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:24.950
Did you get them?

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:26.950
Yes... Here they are!

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:33.710
Confirmed.
You’ve cleared the mission.

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:35.000
Really?!

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:37.210
That’s great, Go!

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:40.710
The token arrived!

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:43.130
That’s only one single token.

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:48.720
As you know, you’ll need to
collect a lot more in order to pass.

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:50.850
I’ll do my best!

00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:54.520
But we needed you guys
to save us again...

00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:56.100
I don’t remember rescuing you.

00:20:56.100 --> 00:21:00.480
We dealt with Hunters
who only think of Pokémon as goods to sell.

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:01.990
That was all.

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:03.360
Right!

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:05.490
Go! Satoshi!

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:07.660
Professor Hodaka!

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:14.210
We’ll take charge of delivering
the Hunters to Ms. Junsa.

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:17.630
What about their Pokémon?

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:21.880
We’ll look after them temporarily,
and later return them to the wild.

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.090
That’s great.

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:23.840
Yeah!

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:29.010
Go, you just get ready for next time.
And don’t worry about anything, okay?

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:32.270
Right!

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:37.230
Go has spectacularly cleared
his first Trial Mission for Project Mew.

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:41.860
Now then, what sort of challenge will he
face in his next mission?

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:09.610
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.610 --> 00:23:10.860
Go!

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:13.910
Blue Pokémania?

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:16.120
Do they like blue Pokémon?

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:18.250
Hey, guys! You should do Aokatsu!

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:19.330
Aokatsu?

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:21.370
It means blue Pokémon-related activities!

00:23:21.370 --> 00:23:22.750
Stop right there!

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:25.960
You haven’t done nearly enough
to call yourself a maniac!

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:27.130
Another one turned up!

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:28.630
What is all this?!

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:31.050
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:33.850
A Clash?! Blue Pokémania!
